From a029f30940e9d24f7f823fe50daad4cbe47671ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:57:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The Barrows doors open, and the six armour sets do what they
 say

Two of round B's four. The puzzle door and the chest's reward interface are next; both need an
interface, which is a different kind of work from this.

THE DOORS OPEN LIKE DOORS. The first version carried the player across the threshold with
~agility_exactmove and never touched the loc, on the grounds that the cache had no open form of the
door. It does: barrows_door_inactive_l/r is the same model with NO OPS on it, which is exactly what
an already-opened door should offer, and it was sitting there unused. So both leaves now swing to
the next tile edge for three ticks and shut behind the player, through
doors/scripts/doubledoors.rs2 - the game's own double-door proc, not a copy of it.

That proc finds a doorway's other leaf by looking for double_door_open_and_close_left/right beside
it, and those two category names are baked into that code. A loc carries exactly one category, so
the thirty-two Barrows door shells wear those and each one names its own handler explicitly, which
is what keeps ~barrows_door_open (and the monster behind it) in front of the generic door trigger.
A shell that ever lost its line would quietly open with no monster, so the battery counts all
thirty-two rather than trusting the category - and says so, because that is exactly the kind of
degradation the dead-click check CANNOT see.

THE SIX ARMOUR SETS, none of which existed in the build. These are a different six from the
brothers' own effects: Ahrim's 25% Strength drain on a magic hit, Dharok's damage scaling, Guthan's
25% heal for the damage dealt, Karil's 25% Agility drain on a ranged hit, Torag's 25% run-energy
drain on a melee hit, and Verac's 25% chance to ignore armour, Defence and protection prayers.

A full set is four pieces from one brother AT ANY STATE OF DEGRADATION, which is why the set is not
tested by item name: a "Dharoks helm 50" is a different obj from a "Dharoks helm" and there are a
hundred and twenty degraded stages. The twenty-four undamaged pieces carry param=barrows_set; every
stage already carried param=fixed pointing back at the piece it repairs into, so ~barrows_set_piece
asks a piece for its set and asks again through param=fixed when the answer is nothing. A 0% piece
resolves the same way and still cannot satisfy a set effect, because the cache gives it no Wear.

DHAROK'S IS THE PLAYER'S VERSION, NOT THE BROTHER'S: his own adds one per cent per hitpoint
missing, the armour's scales with the wearer's MAXIMUM hitpoints too - damage x (1 + missing/100 x
maximum/100), which is +97% at 99 hitpoints with one left and +0% at 10 with one left. That second
term is the whole point and the battery computes both ends.

KARIL'S AND TORAG'S ARE NOT MISSING FROM THE MONSTER PATH. A monster has no Agility and no run
energy, so in Old School they do nothing to one either; both are wired on the player-versus-player
paths, where there is something to drain. Ahrim's DOES work on a monster, because npc_statsub
exists - player_ranged.rs2 already used it for holy water.

Six hooks in all: the three player-versus-npc paths fire ~barrows_set_hit_npc and the three
player-versus-player paths fire ~barrows_set_hit_player, and the battery checks neither calls the
other's. Guthan's answers to any attack, which is what the wiki says, so it is on all six; Ahrim's
asks for a magic hit because his staff can also be swung.

Verified: clean build, rs2check 1701 scripts / 490 configs with 0 ERROR and 0 CHECK, all eleven
batteries green, and barrows_battery.py's 787 checks against 172 mutations - each caught by its own
check.

